# Solutions pages — frozen layout language

Homepage is frozen separately. These five routes are the golden reference set:

- `/solutions` — hub (lighter routing page; not forced to full depth)
- `/product-configurator` — rules / infrastructure reference
- `/3d-product-configurator` — visual / product-led reference
- `/headless-product-configurator` — architecture reference
- `/product-configuration-api` — developer reference

Do not restructure these pages. Only fix bugs, responsive regressions, broken copy, or asset-quality issues.

## Canonical skeleton (depth pages)

```text
Hero
→ Problem / tension
→ Full-width visual
→ Dark mechanism section
→ Capabilities / surfaces
→ Real proof
→ Outcomes
→ Decision support (bridge + FAQ)
→ Final CTA
```

## Locked standards

- **Hero:** split layout (`SolutionHero` / `PageHero`), one strong H1, short lede, 1–2 CTAs, one finished visual (`MediaSlot` or product render).
- **Problem:** two-column editorial compare (`ProblemCompare` or equivalent) — not cards.
- **Full-width visual:** exactly one large cinematic/system image per page via `FullWidthVisual`. If the asset is missing, keep a blank `MediaSlot` placeholder — never invent HTML/CSS artwork.
- **Mechanism:** exactly one primary full-width `ink` band (`SignatureMechanism` / `PcStatement`) with 3-step logic; violet marks resolved / active / synchronized state.
- **Capabilities:** 3–4 unboxed editorial columns (`EditorialColumns`) with small numeric/mono labels.
- **Proof:** exactly one believable proof section — type depends on page:
  - Product Configurator → option graph
  - 3D → live configurator
  - Headless → runtime pipeline
  - API → request/response contract
- **Outcomes:** 3 concise results (`OutcomeGrid`); light cards OK if consistent.
- **Decision support:** related-page `SolutionBridge` + `SeoFaq`.
- **Final CTA:** dark closing band (`SeoCta`) with page-specific wording.

## Consistency locks

- Same section widths / vertical rhythm (`Section` spacing)
- Same hero proportions
- Same dark mechanism treatment
- Same violet meaning: active / resolved / synchronization
- Same capability-column structure
- Same FAQ layout
- Same final CTA / site footer
- Exactly one primary full-width image
- Exactly one primary dark narrative band
- Exactly one proof section

## Hub exception

`/solutions` stays lighter: routing hero, path cards, shared-state ink band, FAQ. Do not force the full nine-block depth onto the hub.

## Shared primitives

Compose with `@repo/ui` + landing patterns (`SolutionHero`, `ProblemCompare`, `FullWidthVisual`, `SignatureMechanism`, `EditorialColumns`, `OutcomeGrid`, `SolutionBridge`, `SeoFaq`, `SeoCta`). Do not invent parallel section recipes.
